* ''The gate's shape'' (the house's lean, talked out 2026-11-13; overrulable, and never the operator's ruling). The house weighed the note against the anon-floor law, under which every vessel MUST always return to its floor (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/dreamnet-rhizome`>> #/the-ground), and against the ward's bound acts (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture#/faces-fleets-and-the-ward`>>), and leans to four lines; the browser stands built as leaned, and the fourth line's census reaches the browser's burn primitives alone.
*# ''Custody held asks the passphrase.'' Where the vessel holds custody (a first passphrase set, or a face joined), the reset asks that passphrase through the ceremony document before anything burns.
*# ''A bare floor takes the typed phrase.'' At a bare floor with nothing sealed, the typed phrase suffices.
*# ''No house door gates the platform.'' A holder who lost the passphrase keeps the platform's own site-data clear, which no house door can gate, so the return to the floor stays whole.
*# ''The class reads wider than reset.'' Any door that destroys a place or a face on a device, on any vessel, takes the gate by default, and so does its UI twin.

